cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this test suite, please cite it as below."
title: "IEC 61131-3 conformance traces: an open, runtime-agnostic test suite for Structured Text runtimes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Celles
    given-names: Sébastien
    email: s.celles@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9987-4338"
repository-code: "https://github.com/s-celles/iec61131-conformance"
license: CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - IEC 61131-3
  - Structured Text
  - PLC
  - conformance testing
  - differential testing
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Plain Structured Text programs paired with plain-text expected input/output
  traces, one record per scan cycle, derived from IEC 61131-3 (editions 2
  and 3) by an AI assistant and not checked against the standard's text, with harnesses for IronPLC, matiec, OpenPLC's
  matiec fork, STruC++, RuSTy, 4diac, rk and truST, recorded differential results, a Lean 4
  model of the standard function blocks from which the expected traces are
  proved to follow, and monitors of the edition 2 block rules.
  Conflicts of interest and AI assistance are declared at
  https://s-celles.github.io/iec61131-conformance/conflict-of-interest/.
date-released: 2026-11-01
version: 0.1.0
